  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;token&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;auth&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;split&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;];&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;try&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;jwt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;verify&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;token&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ACCESS_TOKEN_SECRET&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nx"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;msg&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;`Hello &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;sub&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;catch &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nx"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;401&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;send&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Invalid or expired access token&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ---------- Logout (revoke refresh token) ----------&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;app&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;post&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;/logout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;req&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;refreshTokenJti&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;req&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;cookies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;refreshToken&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;refreshTokenJti&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;redisClient&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;del&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;refreshTokenJti&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nx"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;clearCookie&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;refreshToken&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;httpOnly&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;secure&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;sameSite&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;strict&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nx"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;send&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Logged out&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;async &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;redisClient&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;connect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nx"&gt;app&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;listen&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;3000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;log&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Secure server on :3000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;));&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;})();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What changed?&lt;/strong&gt;  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Short‑lived access token&lt;/strong&gt; (5 min) lives only in memory; stealing it gives a tiny window.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Refresh token&lt;/strong&gt; is a random identifier (&lt;code&gt;jti&lt;/code&gt;) stored in an &lt;strong&gt;httpOnly&lt;/strong&gt; cookie—JavaScript can’t read it, mitigating XSS.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Refresh token rotation&lt;/strong&gt;: on each use we delete the old jti and issue a new one, turning token‑theft into a race condition the attacker almost certainly loses.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Secrets&lt;/strong&gt; are pulled from environment variables, not baked into source.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Logout&lt;/strong&gt; simply revokes the refresh token in Redis, instantly killing the ability to get new access tokens.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you wanted to add &lt;strong&gt;OAuth&lt;/strong&gt; (Google, GitHub, etc.), you’d replace the &lt;code&gt;/login&lt;/code&gt; handler with the provider’s redirect flow, exchange the auth code for tokens, then issue your own refresh/access pair exactly as shown. The core idea stays the same: &lt;em&gt;trust the provider for identity, but manage your own session tokens&lt;/em&gt;.  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Why This New Power Matters
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Now you can build APIs that feel like they’re guarded by the Agents from &lt;em&gt;The Matrix&lt;/em&gt;—fast, stateless, yet with a tight inner circle that’s hard to breach.  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Frontend SPA devs&lt;/strong&gt; can keep the access token in a React state hook or a Vuex store, knowing it’ll expire quickly and won’t survive a page refresh unless they hit &lt;code&gt;/token&lt;/code&gt;.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Server‑side rendered apps&lt;/strong&gt; can still use classic &lt;code&gt;express-session&lt;/code&gt; for CSRF tokens while relying on JWTs for API calls.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Micro‑service architectures&lt;/strong&gt; gain stateless validation (no need to hit a session store on every request) while still being able to revoke misbehaving clients instantly via the refresh‑token revocation list.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In short: you get the best of both worlds—security without sacrificing developer ergonomics.  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Your Turn
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Try swapping the naïve JWT implementation in your own project for the layered version above. Play with the refresh‑token rotation: deliberately steal a cookie (you can’t, but imagine) and see how fast the window closes.  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Challenge:&lt;/strong&gt; Add a third‑party OAuth provider (Google works nicely) to the &lt;code&gt;/login&lt;/code&gt; route, then issue your own refresh/access tokens after the provider returns the user info. Share your snippet in the comments—I’d love to see how you wired it up!  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Happy hacking, and may your tokens stay short‑lived and your cookies stay httpOnly! 🚀&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What is React?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;React is a front-end JavaScript library.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;React was developed by the Facebook Software Engineer Jordan Walke.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;React is also known as React.js or ReactJS.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;React is a tool for building UI components.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How does React Work?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;React creates a VIRTUAL DOM in memory.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Instead of manipulating the browser's DOM directly, React creates a virtual DOM in memory, where it does all the necessary manipulating, before making the changes in the browser DOM.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;React only changes what needs to be changed!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;React finds out what changes have been made, and changes only what needs to be changed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You will learn the various aspects of how React does this in the rest of this tutorial.&lt;br&gt;
